# Codex CLI (~/.codex). Same policy as ~/.claude above — track only curated
# config — but INVERTED to default-deny: ~/.codex interleaves multi-GB SQLite
# state (logs_2.sqlite is 2+ GB), live secrets (auth.json), session history, and
# 250+ ephemeral [projects] trust blocks in config.toml right alongside the few
# curated files. So we ignore the whole tree and allow-list only the portable,
# authored config: AGENTS.md (the CLAUDE.md analog) and the ship agent
# definitions. Skills are deliberately NOT tracked — ~/.codex/skills holds the
# superpowers port plus Codex's shipped system skills, none of it authored here.
# config.toml is deliberately NOT tracked — it is ~95% per-machine project-trust
# state plus machine-specific paths (notify, hooks); curate a portable subset by
# hand if it is ever needed.
.codex/**
!.codex
!.codex/AGENTS.md
!.codex/agents
!.codex/agents/**

